# Example .env for the ETL + viz stack. Copy to .env and fill in.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# NOTHING here must be committed: .env is gitignored (and the real data and
# credentials stay out of git per AGENTS.md). This file only documents the
# variables the repo reads.

# --- Dev-host database (the only var the pipeline strictly needs) ------------
# The ETL (etl/config.py) and the viz app (viz/data.py) load this via
# python-dotenv from the repo-root .env. Two sane values:
#
# * dev host PostGIS (pipeline role with write rights):
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/energy_de
#
# * or the containerized db published on POSTGRES_PORT (see below):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://etl:etl@localhost:5433/energy_de

# --- Optional: read-only role for the viz app ---------------------------------
# The app falls back to DATABASE_URL on the dev host, but connecting as the
# read-only viz_reader (the SQL seam provisions it — see docs/containerization.md)
# is the safe default and the path used in the container.
# VIZ_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://viz_reader:viz@localhost:5432/energy_de

# --- Compose / seed / smoke knobs (read by scripts/*.sh + compose.yaml) -------
# Only needed to override the documented defaults; the defaults are shown to
# the right as reminders.
# ETL_DATA_VOLUME=etl_data          # detached data volume (data/ + docker.env)
# POSTGRES_PORT=5433                # host port for the db service
# VIZ_PORT=8501                     # host port for the Streamlit viz service
# VIZ_USER=viz_reader               # read-only role the app connects as
# VIZ_PASSWORD=viz                  # must match docker/viz_reader.sql (coupled pair)
# DB_HOST=db                        # seed: host written into docker.env
# DB_PORT=5432
# DB_USER=etl
# DB_PASSWORD=etl
# DB_NAME=energy_de